You have learned to block incoming blows with your offhand weapon.

When dual wielding, your defense is increased by [22, 30, 36, 41, 45 (TL1-5; DEX 100; CUN 100)].

Up to [1.0, 1.3, 1.7, 2.0, 2.3 (DEX 10-100; CUN 10-100)] times a turn, you have a [38%, 54%, 64%, 70%, 75% (TL1-5; DEX 100; CUN 100)] chance to parry up to 0 damage (based on your your offhand weapon damage) from a melee attack.

A successful parry reduces damage like armour (before any attack multipliers) and prevents critical strikes.  Partial parries have a proportionally reduced chance to succeed.  It is difficult to parry attacks from unseen attackers and you cannot parry with a mindstar.

The defense and chance to parry improve with Dexterity.  The number of parries increases with Cunning.
